  "answer_markdown": "To achieve both **automatic user joining** and **sign-in without separate password credentials**, the following applies based on Mistral's plans and requirements for a verified domain:\n\n1. **Automatic user joining (via email domain authentication)**\n   - Supported on **Team plans and above** [1].\n   - Requires a **verified domain** [1][4][6].\n   - Users with matching domain emails can join automatically from [Join Organization](https://admin.mistral.ai/join) [1][4].\n   - Users still **create and manage their own credentials** (email + password) [1].\n\n2. **Sign-in without separate password credentials (via SSO)**\n   - Supported on **Enterprise plans** [1].\n   - Requires a **verified domain** and **SAML SSO configuration** [3][5][6].\n   - Users sign in using **corporate credentials** (e.g., Okta, Azure AD) instead of a Mistral password [3][5].\n\n### Key Requirements for Both Features\n- A **verified domain** is mandatory for both mechanisms [1][3][4][6].\n- **Email domain authentication** enables automatic joining but **not passwordless sign-in** [1].\n- **SSO** enables passwordless sign-in but requires **Enterprise plans** [1][3].\n\n### How to Enable Email Domain Authentication (Automatic Joining)\n```\n1. Navigate to **Administration › Settings** in the [Admin panel](https://admin.mistral.ai).\n2. Under **Email domain authentication**, toggle it **on**.\n3. Select the default role for auto-joined users (e.g., **Member**).\n```\n[4]\n\n### How to Configure SSO (Passwordless Sign-In)\n1. Verify your domain via DNS records.\n2. Configure SAML SSO with your IdP (e.g., Okta, Azure AD) [3].\n3. Ensure the domain is marked as **Verified** in Organization Settings [5].\n\n**Note:** If only **Team plans** are available, **SSO (passwordless sign-in) is not supported**—users must use email/password credentials [1].",
