{
  "answer_markdown": "To achieve both **automatic Organization joining** and **sign-in without separate password credentials**, the following mechanisms and plans are required, along with their domain verification prerequisites:\n\n### 1. **Automatic Organization Joining (Email Domain Authentication)**\n- **Supported Plans**: Team and above [1].\n- **Requirements**:\n  - A **verified domain** (via DNS TXT record) [1][5].\n  - Enable **Discoverable** for the verified domain in the Admin Panel [1].\n  - Users with matching email addresses can join automatically, but **still create and manage their own credentials** (email/password) [1].\n\n### 2. **Sign-in Without Separate Password Credentials (SSO)**\n- **Supported Plans**: Enterprise only [7].\n- **Requirements**:\n  - A **verified domain** [5][7].\n  - SAML SSO configuration with an IdP (e.g., Okta, Azure AD) [7].\n  - Users sign in via corporate credentials without needing Mistral-specific passwords [7].\n\n### Key Differences\n- **Email Domain Authentication** (Team+) only controls **Organization membership** (auto-joining), not authentication [1].\n- **SSO** (Enterprise) replaces password-based sign-in entirely with corporate credentials [7].\n\n### Domain Verification\nBoth features require a **verified domain** via DNS TXT record [1][5][7].\n\n> **Note**: No single plan supports both mechanisms simultaneously; SSO requires Enterprise, while auto-joining is available on Team plans.\n\n",
