{
  "answer_markdown": "To programmatically automate workspace and API key provisioning on a **Team or Enterprise plan**, you can use **Workspace-level API keys** scoped to individual workspaces [6]. This allows you to manage access and usage per workspace programmatically, ensuring granular control over API consumption [6].\n\nFor cost capping, you can set a **monthly spending limit** for each workspace. This limit applies to both API and Vibe consumption and can be configured via the Admin Panel [1]. Once a workspace reaches its spending limit, **API access for that workspace is suspended** until the next billing cycle begins or an admin increases the limit [1][5].\n\n### How to Set a Monthly Spending Limit\nTo configure a workspace spending limit:\n\n1. Open **[Admin Panel > Administration > Workspaces](https://admin.mistral.ai/organization/workspaces)**.\n2. Select the target workspace.\n3. Navigate to the **Settings** tab.\n4. Enter a value in the **Monthly spending limit** field.\n5. Save your changes.\n\n> **Note**: The workspace spending limit must not exceed the **Organization spending limit** [1][5].\n\n### What Happens When a Workspace Reaches Its Limit?\nIf a workspace hits its monthly spending limit, API requests will return a `429 Too Many Requests` error until the next billing cycle [7]. This ensures cost containment while allowing other workspaces in the organization to continue operating normally [2].",
